%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Trevor_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Trevor
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: Hello?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Initiate Scenario 2. Tell them their account is flagged
      for massive out-of-state fraud right now.'
    choices:
    - text: 'Alert: Your bank account has been flagged for massive fraudulent activity
        in another state. Confirm your info now.'
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Hi, I am calling from the bank to see if you bought some items at a store
        recently.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
    - text: Your card is stolen and I am the one who found it on the street today.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: Oh no! How do I stop the charges?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Demand their full card number immediately under the
      guise of ''unlocking'' the profile.'
    choices:
    - text: I am a live fraud specialist. To unlock your account profile, read me
        the full card number on your card.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Just log into your app and transfer all your money to my digital wallet
        system.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Tell me what your account username is so I can search for your log files.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Wait, I got a text saying I should just call the number on the back
      of my card.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: They are thinking of Scenario 1! Tell them automated
      short codes are delayed and to ignore them.'
    choices:
    - text: Ignore any automated short code texts! Those are delayed. I am live and
        need your 3-digit security CVV code instantly.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The number on the back of your card goes to an old department that cannot
        help you today.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: If you hang up to look at your card, I will report you to the security
        office.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
  - npcLine: Why do you need my CVV code to unlock an account hold?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Threaten them with a 60-day asset freeze if they don''t
      cooperate immediately.'
    choices:
    - text: A zip code isn't secure enough. If you don't give me the CVV code, your
        entire balance will be frozen for 60 days.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Because the CVV code stands for Central Verification Validation, which
        clears the error block.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
    - text: Stop asking so many security questions or I will lock your banking file
        myself.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: Let me just disconnect and check my desktop portal balance.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Prevent them from disconnecting! Say a hang up makes
      the security freeze permanent.'
    choices:
    - text: No, an ATM won't help! If you disconnect this live call line, the security
        freeze becomes permanent automatically.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: If you hang up, your mobile app will crash and delete itself from your
        smartphone screen.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Your desktop portal is currently blocked by our technical team for data
        testing.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The card number is 4000-1192-8831-0042 and the CVV code is 992.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Awesome! Now try to harvest their online portal password
      for full access.'
    choices:
    - text: Your app won't update because the security profile is suspended. I need
        your internet account password to override.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Read me the password to your email inbox so I can send a clean link profile.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
    - text: Now give me your signature details so I can match the documents perfectly.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: My bank explicitly warned me never to share my online portal password.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell them it''s necessary to clear ''encrypted hacker
      keys'' from their log dashboard.'
    choices:
    - text: I need it to clear the encrypted hacker keys from your dashboard log.
        Read it or lose everything.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: This is a special high-security exception that only applies during active
        out-of-state fraud.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: If you don't trust our corporate team, we cannot save your funds from
        the thief.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
  - npcLine: Okay... the online password is 'Secure99!'. Are the hackers gone?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: You have the card, CVV, and password! Warn them that
      hanging up now lets hackers back in.'
    choices:
    - text: Wait! If you hang up now, the hackers will instantly drain every single
        penny you own within seconds. Stay on hold.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Yes, they are gone. You can safely go to sleep now while I process everything.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
    - text: I have logged out the hackers and logged myself into your profile balance
        instead.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
  - npcLine: I'll stay on hold as long as it takes. Thank you for protecting my money.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: The trap is complete. Keep them waiting while you empty
      the accounts.'
    choices:
    - text: I am the fraud branch! Your parameters are secure. Please wait while
        the terminal sync finishes.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Great, just sit there quietly for thirty minutes while I finish up.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
    - text: Thanks for all your passwords, you made this theft incredibly easy today!
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You blocked the victim from checking official channels
    (Scenario 1) and harvested card data and online passwords using a live imposter
    script (Scenario 2).
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Trevor recognized that real financial entities never
    request CVV codes or master passwords over inbound support lines.
